! Look-ahead timing microbenchmark (docs/microarchitecture_plan.md
! stage 3a): four full-word VFL loads from four different words, then
! the halt. Each load costs 6 I-box cycles of preparation (12 clocks)
! and, by Performance Characteristics table 3, 1.8 + 8*0.6 + 0.6 = 7.2
! us = 24 clocks in the serial arithmetic unit. With the look-ahead
! the four fetches are issued ahead and the E-box is the bottleneck:
! about 12 (first preparation) + 7 (first fetch) + 4*24 = 115 clocks
! plus the halt's own time. Executed one at a time with no overlap the
! same sequence would take about 4*(12 + 7 + 24) = 172. The bound in
! run_tests.sh (140) sits between the two, so it fails if the overlap
! is lost.
START   L(BU,64,8), A
        L(BU,64,8), B
        L(BU,64,8), C
        L(BU,64,8), D
        NOP, 0.0
DONE    BEW, $
A       DD(BU,64,8), 1
B       DD(BU,64,8), 2
C       DD(BU,64,8), 3
D       DD(BU,64,8), 4
        END, START
